    {
      "external_id": "C12-PHY-CH14-14.4-INSTANTANEOUS-ACCELERATION",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xii/physics/c12-phy/ch14",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xii/physics/c12-phy/ch14/u-instantaneous-acceleration",
      "title": "Instantaneous Acceleration",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "bfc68b7f-dac5-5e57-a286-814710fe09bc",
          "pdf_from": 27,
          "pdf_to": 28,
          "note": "Instantaneous Acceleration: a main subheading of 14.4 Simple Harmonic Motion and Uniform Circular Motion, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 27-28."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Acceleration aₚ of the particle at point P is directed towards the centre of the circle as shown in Fig. 14.7. The horizontal component of aₚ is along the diameter. Thus, the acceleration of projection Q is equal to the horizontal component of aₚ."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "a = (a_P)x",
            "text_alt": "a = (aₚ)x"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "a = a_P\\cos\\theta",
            "text_alt": "a = aₚ cosθ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "As a = −x₀ω² (centripetal acceleration) and cos θ = x/x₀."
          },
          {
            "type": "diagram",
            "$asset": "c12-phy-ch14-fig-14-7-acceleration",
            "alt": "The same circle with points A, B and C. The centripetal acceleration ap of P points along PO towards the centre. Its horizontal component a acts on Q along the diameter BA towards O. The angle theta is marked at O and at P, and x is the distance OQ.",
            "caption": "Figure 14.7: Acceleration of the point P and its horizontal component (original drawing after the textbook's Figure 14.7).",
            "side": true
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The negative sign indicates that the direction of acceleration is always directed towards the mean position."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "a = -x_0\\omega^2\\left(\\frac{x}{x_0}\\right) = -\\omega^2 x",
            "text_alt": "a = −x₀ω²(x/x₀) = −ω²x"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "a = -x\\omega^2 \\tag{14.15}",
            "text_alt": "a = −xω²   (14.15)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "As particle is moving in the circle with uniform angular frequency ω, therefore, Eq. (14.15) can be rewritten as;"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "a \\propto -x",
            "text_alt": "a ∝ −x"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "This expression is the mathematical condition of S.H.M i.e., acceleration is directly proportional to the displacement and negative sign shows that its direction is towards mean position, therefore, it is concluded that when a particle is moving along a circumference of a circle then its projection executes S.H.M."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Example 14.3"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A 0.2 kg mass is attached to a spring with a spring constant of 10 N m⁻¹. The mass is displaced by 0.1 m from its equilibrium position and released from rest. Find:"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solution",
            "bold": [
              "Solution"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "(a) acceleration at x = 0.05 m (b) velocity at x = 0.05 m"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "m = 0.2 kg"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "k = 10 N m⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "x₀ = 0.1 m"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Angular frequency ω = ?"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ω = √(k/m) = √(10 N m⁻¹ / 0.2 kg) = √50 = 5√2 rad s⁻¹ ≈ 7.07 rad s⁻¹."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "(a) Acceleration at x = 0.05 m"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "a = −ω²x"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "= −(7.07 rad s⁻¹)² × 0.05 m"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "= −50 × 0.05"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "= −2.5 m s⁻²"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "(b) Velocity at x = 0.05 m"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "v = ω√(x₀² − x²)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "v = 7.07 rad s⁻¹ √((0.1 m)² − (0.05 m)²)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "= 7.07√((0.01) − (0.0025))"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "= √0.0075"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "≈ 7.07 × 0.0866"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "v ≈ 0.612 m s⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The results are: a ≈ −2.5 m s⁻², v ≈ 0.612 m s⁻¹"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
